{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1516914-bygone-bestiary-special-advantages-with-xp","id":1516914,"title":"Bygone Bestiary: Special Advantages with XP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-01T14:13:30-07:00","id":1516914,"title":"Bygone Bestiary: Special Advantages with XP","content":"So, with special-advantages, you can only buy at character-creation, and, starting out with just six seems, well, very limiting, and yes, you can have up to 33 special-advantages, if your ST lets you. So, why not be able to buy special-advantages with XP? To be a dragon, you need like, 50 or 60 points. And why not make it like vampire disciplines; if you have Regrowth at 2pts, why not, with time, get Regrowth at 4pts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T23:41:44-07:00","id":1516946,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree. As Storyteller, I would let Bygone PCs buy Advantages, or at least certain ones, after char-gen, so long as there's a good explanation for it.<br /> <br /> Like, it only makes sense for a Dragon PC to be smaller and weaker to start with. Only to gain greater size, thicker scales, a breath weapon (if they don't start with it), and maybe the ability to shapeshift. Indeed, being able to shapeshift into a smaller form, like that of a normal animal or human, would become increasingly more important to a Dragon PC as they got older, just to be able to go where the other PCs go. You can put a wyrmling under a tarp and maybe pass it off as a beast or a person with leprosy (so long as NPCs aren't allowed to look too closely). A Dragon with multiple points worth of Size isn't even fitting through the doorway, which hampers adventuring.<br /> <br /> Also, for Bygone PCs, the accruing of more Advantages kind of IS their main character progression outlet. In much the way Disciplines are for Vampires and Spheres are for Mages. As those become more adept in their respective supernatural powers, the mythical creature (the Bygone) becomes <i>more mythical</i> as they gain experience. Like a &quot;noble dog&quot; whose main claim to being a Bygone being capability of human speech, that gains more powers related to being a &quot;noble animal&quot;, like a Healing Lick, Mystick Shield, Soul-Sense, or Bond-Sharing.<br /> <br /> It would be kind of a letdown, especially in mixed splat games, if everyone else could funnel XP into cool powers, and your Bygone PC was stuck only raising Attributes, Abilities, and Backgrounds. (What Abilities and Backgrounds your Bygone even qualifies for, at that. Can a creature with no dexterous limbs even gain dots in Melee?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}